  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-1,\\frac{1}{3}}$ given below.\n\n${-1,\\frac{1}{3}}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,3{q}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$q\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$",
  "worked_solution": "The given set contains the roots $q\\in Q$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(q).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${q}_{1}=-1$ and ${q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(q) & =a(q-{q}_{1})(q-{q}_{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (q-(-1))(q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3(q+1)(q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3({q}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3{q}^{2}+2q-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-1,\\frac{1}{3}}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,3{q}^{2}+2q-1=0}\n$$",
